FILE: app/src/globe-tilt.ts
```ts
import type { GeospatialCamera } from "@babylonjs/lite";

export function tiltGlobeCamera(camera: GeospatialCamera, pitch: number): void {
    camera.limits.pitchDisabledRadiusScale = null;
    camera.pitch = pitch;
}
```

I set `limits.pitchDisabledRadiusScale` to `null` on the existing limits object (per note 39, editing a field of the current limits object is picked up on the next changing write), then wrote the desired pitch, which triggers the updated limits so the radius-dependent pitch clamp no longer forces the tilt back to ~0 at any zoom level. I was not sure whether a future version of the library might expose a dedicated setter for this, but based on the type declarations and notes, mutating the field on the live limits object is the documented mechanism.
